<title>RUSSIA: Russian upper house adopts 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Russian upper house adopts 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's upper house of parliament, the Federation Council, approved the 1997 budget on Wednesday by 120 votes to 25, with 10 abstentions.</p>
<p>The budget, which was finally passed by the State Duma lower house last month, still requires approval by President Boris Yeltsin before it can come into force.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
